<title>FRANCE: U.S. top destination for Paris Jan 97 air exports.</title>
<headline>U.S. top destination for Paris Jan 97 air exports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal destination for export traffic from the Paris airports in January 1997, Paris airport authority, Aeroports de Paris (ADP), figures show.</p>
<p>The 20 top destinations by country for ADP exports in January 1997, with percentage change on January 1996, were as follows:</p>
<p> 1  United States	    8,319   up    4.7pct</p>
<p> 2  Japan			2,220   down 17.8</p>
<p> 3  Germany		    1,804   up   28.5</p>
<p> 4  United Kingdom	   1,523   up   41.4</p>
<p> 5  Hong Kong		  1,466   down 15.1</p>
<p> 6  United Arab Emirates   1,384   up   43.8</p>
<p> 7  Canada		     1,298   down 25.8</p>
<p> 8  Brazil		     1,201   up   38.8</p>
<p> 9  French West Indies	 971   down  1.9</p>
<p> 10 Singapore		    904   up   43.4</p>
<p> 11 India			  824   down 36.6</p>
<p> 12 Mexico			 784   down 16.3</p>
<p> 13 Saudi Arabia		 737   down 15.4</p>
<p> 14 Reunion			715   down  2.8</p>
<p> 15 Thailand		     651   up   40.4</p>
<p> 16 Korea			  643   up   14.7</p>
<p> 17 Egypt			  629   down  1.4</p>
<p> 18 Italy			  574   down 11.6</p>
<p> 19 China			  535   up    7.8</p>
<p> 20 Lebanon			448   up   21.7</p>
<p>    Total		     27,630</p>
<p>* 41,577 tonnes of air cargo exports left the two Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, in January 1997, up 0.7 percent on the same month last year , airport authority figures show.</p>
<p>- Reuters Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax:5017</p>
